{:edb/db-before-t 1799 :edb/db-after-t 1800 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535112 50 #inst "2026-10-08T17:08:15.253Z" 13194139535112 true] [17592186147366 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331876 13194139535112 true] [17592186147367 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331890 13194139535112 true] [17592186147368 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331883 13194139535112 true] [17592186147368 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331897 13194139535112 true] [17592186331876 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331877 13194139535112 true] [17592186331876 1089 "q-129215" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331876 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535112 true] [17592186331876 1100 "The intersection of the planes $2x-3z=0$ and $2y-3z-6=0$ is given by the line\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{a}_{1},{a}_{2},0⟩+tb,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2},$ and find a possible direction vector $b.$" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331876 1113 #uuid "583166f3-f984-5b08-b009-d0467651a92a" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331876 1145 "We're given that there exists a point on the line where $z=0.$ Substituting this to the first equation gives\n\n$$\n2x-0=0\\,⟹\\,x=0,\n$$\n\nand substituting $z=0$ into the second equation gives\n\n$$\n2y-0-6=0\\,⟹\\,y=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=⟨0,3,0⟩$ is a position vector of a point on the line.\n\nNext, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $2x-3z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨2,0,-3⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2y-3z-6=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,2,-3⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨2,0,-3⟩\\times ⟨0,2,-3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =6i+6j+4k \\\\  & =⟨6,6,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the equation of the line is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+tb \\\\ r(t) & =⟨0,3,0⟩+t⟨6,6,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then, ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=0+3=3,$ and $b=⟨6,6,4⟩.$" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331878 13194139535112 true] [17592186331877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331879 13194139535112 true] [17592186331877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331880 13194139535112 true] [17592186331877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331881 13194139535112 true] [17592186331877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331882 13194139535112 true] [17592186331877 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535112 true] [17592186331877 1041 "selection" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331877 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331882 13194139535112 true] [17592186331877 1110 #uuid "639a9cca-ac75-56eb-870d-145fc313d159" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331878 1034 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-3,\\,b=⟨6,6,-4⟩" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331878 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535112 true] [17592186331878 1111 #uuid "8a8f7a45-4d82-58b9-bd8a-4a39eb05db24" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331879 1034 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=12,\\,b=⟨6,4,-6⟩" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331879 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535112 true] [17592186331879 1111 #uuid "c7782099-a0fd-53c6-86da-c019401e1704" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331880 1034 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=3,\\,b=⟨6,4,-6⟩" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331880 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535112 true] [17592186331880 1111 #uuid "49ef3c52-2524-518f-b2f3-1a0a54daaf75" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331881 1034 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=6,\\,b=⟨4,6,6⟩" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331881 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535112 true] [17592186331881 1111 #uuid "958eab3e-848e-5daa-8090-2f55167ef79a" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331882 1034 "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=3,\\,b=⟨6,6,4⟩" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331882 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535112 true] [17592186331882 1111 #uuid "b33ba095-c0ae-5126-8eb9-0d3719014ba4" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331883 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331884 13194139535112 true] [17592186331883 1089 "q-129241" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331883 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535112 true] [17592186331883 1100 "Given the two planes $x-3y+2z=0$ and $x-2y+5=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The normal vectors of the planes are parallel.\n- The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$\n- The planes intersect on a line." 13194139535112 true] [17592186331883 1113 #uuid "959d7c1a-33e8-592b-b5a5-d7f6a288fc45" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331883 1145 "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x-3y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,-3,2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x-2y+5=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-2,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,-2,1⟩\\times ⟨1,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =4i+2j+k \\\\  & =⟨4,2,1⟩\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." 13194139535112 true] [17592186331884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331885 13194139535112 true] [17592186331884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331886 13194139535112 true] [17592186331884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331887 13194139535112 true] [17592186331884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331888 13194139535112 true] [17592186331884 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331889 13194139535112 true] [17592186331884 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535112 true] [17592186331884 1041 "selection" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331884 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331888 13194139535112 true] [17592186331884 1110 #uuid "b141f848-4c27-5b0c-bf2a-351e8d6af56b" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331885 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331885 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535112 true] [17592186331885 1111 #uuid "c3b9f991-4144-574d-b26f-5126b1b33b4c" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331886 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331886 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535112 true] [17592186331886 1111 #uuid "b1ec36b8-e877-5158-9f63-24320f697d1f" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331887 1034 "I only" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331887 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535112 true] [17592186331887 1111 #uuid "a5918a05-fcd8-5042-af53-53d9846fbcdc" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331888 1034 "III only" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331888 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535112 true] [17592186331888 1111 #uuid "d66d9ffa-275f-5859-b1ba-449c843e4255" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331889 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331889 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535112 true] [17592186331889 1111 #uuid "5d743de0-62e6-5fc0-80b4-ce5ef89010b1" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331890 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331891 13194139535112 true] [17592186331890 1089 "q-71270" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331890 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535112 true] [17592186331890 1100 "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the planes $y=-2$ and $x=z-1.$" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331890 1113 #uuid "07f0b1a9-ab3f-550e-aed9-fa24adcc5d73" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331890 1145 "First, notice that: \n\n- For the plane $y=-2$, a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨0,1,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x=z-1$ (or $x-z+1=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,0,-1⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨0,1,0⟩\\times ⟨1,0,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-i-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331891 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331892 13194139535112 true] [17592186331891 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331893 13194139535112 true] [17592186331891 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331894 13194139535112 true] [17592186331891 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331895 13194139535112 true] [17592186331891 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331896 13194139535112 true] [17592186331891 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535112 true] [17592186331891 1041 "selection" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331891 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331893 13194139535112 true] [17592186331891 1110 #uuid "85eebecb-b9cc-579b-ad41-89b7d00bf833" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331892 1034 "⟨-1,1,-1⟩" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331892 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535112 true] [17592186331892 1111 #uuid "9392e3be-7aa7-5abd-a322-def83c3cac05" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331893 1034 "⟨-1,0,-1⟩" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331893 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535112 true] [17592186331893 1111 #uuid "a3000ea4-aee3-503f-b65c-4f7d296ec66d" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331894 1034 "⟨-1,0,1⟩" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331894 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535112 true] [17592186331894 1111 #uuid "d138b3b6-10ad-5baa-8d40-161716166c68" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331895 1034 "⟨0,1,0⟩" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331895 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535112 true] [17592186331895 1111 #uuid "59a70a86-1425-531c-a9b0-57b66d585fe9" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331896 1034 "⟨1,0,-1⟩" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331896 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535112 true] [17592186331896 1111 #uuid "3ce81cc0-c749-5b7b-aae8-7da401f5959e" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331897 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331898 13194139535112 true] [17592186331897 1089 "q-71464" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331897 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535112 true] [17592186331897 1100 "Given the two planes $y-z=1$ and $2x+z=3$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨1,-2,-2⟩.$\n- The normal vectors of the planes are parallel.\n- The planes intersect on a line." 13194139535112 true] [17592186331897 1113 #uuid "e907b0e4-0542-5071-9a1e-54575ac732d3" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331897 1145 "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $y-z=1,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨0,1,-1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2x+z=3,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨2,0,1⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨0,1,-1⟩\\times ⟨2,0,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i-2j-2k \\\\  & =⟨1,-2,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and  III are true." 13194139535112 true] [17592186331898 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331899 13194139535112 true] [17592186331898 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331900 13194139535112 true] [17592186331898 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331901 13194139535112 true] [17592186331898 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331902 13194139535112 true] [17592186331898 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331903 13194139535112 true] [17592186331898 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535112 true] [17592186331898 1041 "selection" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331898 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331899 13194139535112 true] [17592186331898 1110 #uuid "9acc8d8c-164b-5548-ba64-8644a3a2b0f4" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331899 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331899 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535112 true] [17592186331899 1111 #uuid "78635d73-fef2-5c84-92bf-06f3c8b0a8de" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331900 1034 "I only" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331900 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535112 true] [17592186331900 1111 #uuid "100aa6e1-f88f-562d-8158-55ec968a394b" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331901 1034 "III only" 13194139535112 true] [17592186331901 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535112 true] [17592186331901 1111 #u